# PostgreSQL Integration Rules

## 🔴 MANDATORY - CHECK FIRST
**Before ANY PostgreSQL integration:**
- [ ] Database connection string: `postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database`
- [ ] Choose ORM: Prisma (recommended), Drizzle, or raw SQL
- [ ] Use server components for database operations
- [ ] Configure connection pooling for production

## 🐘 CONNECTION SETUP
```typescript
// Environment variables
POSTGRES_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/mydb"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/mydb" // For migrations

// Prisma setup
npx prisma init
npx prisma db push
npx prisma generate
```

## 🗂️ SCHEMA DEFINITION
```typescript
// schema.prisma
model User {
  id        Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
  email     String   @unique
  name      String?
  posts     Post[]
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt
}

model Post {
  id       Int    @id @default(autoincrement())
  title    String
  content  String?
  author   User   @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id])
  authorId Int
}
```

## 🔧 CRUD OPERATIONS
```typescript
// Server component with database operations
import { prisma } from '@/lib/prisma';

async function UsersList() {
  const users = await prisma.user.findMany({
    include: { posts: true },
    orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' }
  });
  
  return (
    <div>
      {users.map(user => (
        <UserCard key={user.id} user={user} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}

// API route for mutations
export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const data = await request.json();
  
  const user = await prisma.user.create({
    data: {
      email: data.email,
      name: data.name
    }
  });
  
  return Response.json(user);
}
```

## 🚀 PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION
- **Indexing**: Create indexes on frequently queried columns
- **Pagination**: Use cursor-based pagination for large datasets  
- **Relationships**: Use `include` and `select` judiciously
- **Connection Pooling**: Configure max connections appropriately
- **Query Optimization**: Use EXPLAIN ANALYZE for slow queries

## 🔐 SECURITY BEST PRACTICES
```typescript
// Input validation with Zod
import { z } from 'zod';

const createUserSchema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email(),
  name: z.string().min(1).max(100)
});

// Validate before database operations
const validatedData = createUserSchema.parse(requestData);
```

## 📊 ADVANCED FEATURES
- **JSON Support**: Store and query JSON data types
- **Full-text Search**: Use PostgreSQL's built-in search capabilities
- **Triggers**: Implement business logic at database level
- **Extensions**: Leverage PostGIS, UUID, etc.
- **Transactions**: Use for data consistency

## 🔄 MIGRATIONS
```bash
# Create and apply migrations
npx prisma migrate dev --name add-user-model
npx prisma migrate deploy # Production

# Reset database (development only)
npx prisma migrate reset
```

## 🚨 ERROR HANDLING
```typescript
// Handle database errors gracefully
try {
  const result = await prisma.user.create(data);
  return result;
} catch (error) {
  if (error.code === 'P2002') {
    throw new Error('Email already exists');
  }
  console.error('Database error:', error);
  throw new Error('Database operation failed');
}
```